{"additions":649,"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"Closes #209\n\n## Changes\n\n- An issue or PR assigned to the viewer, or a PR waiting for their review, gets a yellow state icon and the viewer's login in bold yellow — in the rows and in the detail header's `Assignees:` / `Reviewers:` line (case-insensitive match).\n- `m` on either list keeps only those items (`GitHub · mine` in the header, `Only items for @td72 (m shows all)` in the status bar). It is a local filter over the fetched lists — no request — applied once the signed-in login is known. `github-mine-only \"on\"` starts the page that way.\n- The GitHub page now resolves the viewer like the Projects page does (`github-login`, else `gh config get`; `viewer::resolve`) and hands it to both lists and both detail panes.\n- Projects board: the viewer's cards get the same icon color and bold login (the table's Assignees cell too), and the Projects detail header highlights them as well.\n- `github-show-closed` and `github-mine-only` share one on / off parser.\n- Tests: the people highlight, the `m` toggle in the page state (viewer arriving later, config start), board cards (styles survive truncation), config validation.\n- README en/ja, the guide (views-github, views-projects, config-reference en/ja), the GitHub issue tape (`m` on and off) and the two GitHub GIFs.\n\n## Screenshot\n\n![github issue demo](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/td72/vig/feat/highlight-mine/assets/demo-github-issue.gif)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01N7wFSHbpTzvkK6WS1CRS7b","changedFiles":27,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-11-05T08:47:00Z","deletions":81,"headRefName":"feat/highlight-mine","isDraft":true,"labels":[],"number":214,"reviewDecision":"","reviewRequests":[],"reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-05T08:51:42Z","conclusion"